{
  "stage": 5,
  "repo": "fde-05-mcp-legacy-bridge",
  "title": "MCP & Legacy System Integration",
  "tagline": "A Model Context Protocol server written on raw JSON-RPC 2.0 that lets an agent call a 2004-era SOAP system and SAP, with schema checks, safe XML, and rate limits the old system can survive.",
  "why": "Agents need tools, and in a large company the tools are SOAP services, SAP OData endpoints and systems that fall over at ten requests a second. An SDK hides the protocol; an FDE has to debug it at the wire. This repo implements MCP directly on JSON-RPC, validates every argument before it reaches the legacy system, translates JSON to SOAP and back without injection holes, and throttles calls so the agent cannot take the mainframe down.",
  "covers": [
    "MCP on raw JSON-RPC 2.0: initialize, ping, tools/list, tools/call, notifications, batches, error codes -32700 / -32600 / -32601 / -32602 / -32002",
    "Safe writes: legacy_update_customer is two-step (preview diff, then commit with a one-use, 60-second confirm token), needs an idempotency key, uses optimistic locking on the record version, and routes big credit-limit jumps to a human",
    "stdio transport: fde-05-mcp-legacy-bridge serve works with any MCP client",
    "Input-schema validation before any legacy call (required, types, pattern, no extra args)",
    "SOAP 1.1: envelope builder with escaped values and validated element names; strict XML reader that refuses DOCTYPE (no XXE); Fault handling",
    "Per-tool token bucket rate limiting, plus retry planning with full-jitter backoff, Retry-After and a deadline",
    "SAP OData v2 URL builder: typed filters, quote escaping, $top cap, column checks"
  ],
  "gaps": [
    "The SOAP backend is an in-process mock (stateful, so writes are real in the demo); production needs an HTTP client and the real WSDL",
    "No headless-browser fallback for systems with no API",
    "No real SAP RFC / BAPI or Oracle EBS connector; OData URL building only",
    "No Streamable HTTP transport or OAuth for the MCP server (stdio only)"
  ],
  "extra_md": "## Use it from an MCP client\n\n```bash\ncargo build --release\n# then point your client at the binary, e.g. Claude Code:\nclaude mcp add legacy-bridge -- $(pwd)/target/release/fde-05-mcp-legacy-bridge serve\n```\n\nOr talk to it by hand:\n\n```bash\nprintf '%s\\n' '{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"initialize\",\"params\":{}}' \\\n  '{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":2,\"method\":\"tools/call\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"legacy_get_customer\",\"arguments\":{\"customer_id\":\"C-1001\"}}}' \\\n  | cargo run -q -- serve\n```",
